.\" EazyMake manual page -- ezmk.toml(5)
.\" Written for EazyMake 1.4.3.
.\" Keep in sync with src/config.cpp: run scripts/check_man_sync.py before
.\" committing changes to this file or to the parser.
.TH EZMK.TOML 5 "2026-10-02" "EazyMake 1.4.5" "File Formats"
.\" Disable hyphenation: this page is full of copy-pasteable keys and flags.
.nh
.SH NAME
ezmk.toml \- EazyMake project configuration file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ezmk.toml
is the single configuration file of an EazyMake project: it declares what to
build, how to compile and link it, which packages it depends on, how it is
tested and installed, and which Lua hooks run around the build.
.PP
Commands look for the file in the current directory and then walk up at most
.B 5
parent directories, so
.B ezmk build
works from a source subdirectory. A directory without
.B ezmk.toml
is not a project; a directory with only
.B ezmk\-workspace.toml
is a workspace container (see
.BR ezmk (1)).
.PP
Only
.B [project].version
is mandatory. Every other key is optional and has a default; keys that
EazyMake does not know are ignored, so a configuration can be shared with
other tools without breaking the build. An invalid value for a known key is
an error, not a warning.
.SH FILE FORMAT
The file is TOML. Values used by EazyMake are strings, integers, booleans and
arrays of strings; unsupported shapes (for example a table where an array is
expected) are configuration errors.
.PP
Boolean
.B false
and an empty string count as "not set" for several keys: an explicitly empty
.B src_dirs
is an error, while an empty
.B include_dirs
or
.B [test].dirs
silently falls back to its default.
.SH SECTIONS
.SS [project]
.TP
.B name
String, optional. Project name, used for the artifact name and for the
.B EZMK_PROJECT_NAME
macro. Only
.B version
is validated, so a missing
.B name
degrades quietly rather than failing the build.
.TP
.B version
String, required (for example
.BR 0.1.0 ).
Feeds the
.B EZMK_PROJECT_VERSION
macro.
.TP
.B type
String, optional, one of
.BR executable " (default), " static ", " shared " or " utils .
The type decides which sources are required and where artifacts are installed.
.TP
.B language
String, optional, default
.BR "C++17" .
The language standard, written as
.BR C++17 ", " C11 ", " GNUCPP17
and so on;
.BR C++ ", " CXX " and " CPP
are interchangeable and matching is case\-insensitive. Two bound forms are
accepted:
.B >=C++11
(a lower bound only) and
.BR C++11..C++17
(minimum and maximum, where the maximum is metadata: compilation always uses
the minimum). A lone
.B >
is rejected, as is a reversed range.
.TP
.B stdlib
String, optional, default
.BR libstdc++ .
Standard library of a package. Aliases are normalized:
.BR glibcxx " and " gnu
mean
.BR libstdc++ ,
.B llvm
means
.BR libc++ .
.TP
.B header_only
Boolean, optional, default
.BR false .
Package setting: install
.B include/
and skip compilation entirely.
.TP
.B precompiled
Boolean, optional, default
.BR false .
Package setting: use the archives in
.B lib/
instead of compiling sources.
.TP
.B precompiled_strict
Boolean, optional, default
.BR false .
Package setting: refuse an ABI\-unsafe toolchain fallback and fail instead of
warning.
.SS [compile]
.TP
.B flags
Array of strings, optional, default empty. Compiler flags. Common GCC and
Clang flags are translated for MSVC.
.TP
.B msvc_flags
Array of strings, optional, default empty. Appended verbatim, and only when
the MSVC toolchain is used.
.TP
.B include_dirs
Array of strings, optional, default
.BR ["include"] .
.B \-I
search paths, relative to the project root. The project's
.B include/
directory is always added when it exists, whether or not it is listed here.
.TP
.B src_dirs
Array of strings, optional, default
.BR ["src"] .
Directories scanned for source files. An explicitly empty array is an error. Only files directly inside each directory are scanned by default; an entry ending in /** is searched recursively.
.TP
.B ezmk_macros
Boolean, optional, default
.BR true .
Inject the standard macros
.BR EZMK ", " EZMK_VERSION ", " EZMK_PROJECT_NAME ", " EZMK_PROJECT_VERSION ,
.BR EZMK_PROJECT_TYPE ", " EZMK_LANG " and " EZMK_STDLIB .
.TP
.B compile_commands
Boolean, optional, default
.BR false .
Write
.B compile_commands.json
after a successful link.
.TP
.B default_profile
String, optional, default empty. Profile applied when
.B \-\-profile
is not given. A plain
.B ezmk build
merges that profile; when empty, no profile is applied.
.TP
.B deterministic
Boolean, optional, default
.BR false .
Reproducible builds: see
.BR "DETERMINISTIC BUILDS" .
.TP
.B source_date_epoch
Integer, optional, default
.BR 0 .
Timestamp for deterministic builds;
.B 0
means "resolve automatically" and a negative value is rejected.
.TP
.B include_dir
String, deprecated. The old singular form of
.BR include_dirs .
When present it is mapped to
.BR include_dirs .
.SS [compile.macros]
A table of macro names to values, compiled into
.BR \-D
flags:
.TP
.B NAME = \(dqtext\(dq
Becomes
.BR NAME="text" .
.TP
.B "NAME = 42"
Becomes
.BR NAME=42 .
.TP
.B "NAME = true"
Becomes
.BR NAME=1 ;
.B false
emits nothing.
.TP
.B NAME = \(dq\(dq
Defines the symbol without a value.
.PP
Names must be valid C identifiers (a letter or underscore followed by letters,
digits or underscores).
Later definitions win, so the precedence is: standard
.B EZMK_*
macros, then
.B \-D
entries in
.BR flags ,
then
.BR [compile.macros] ,
then macros generated for missing
.B want
dependencies.
.SS [compile.profile.<name>]
A named build profile:
.TP
.B flags
Array of strings, optional. Appended after the base
.BR [compile].flags .
.TP
.B msvc_flags
Array of strings, optional. Appended after the base MSVC flags.
.TP
.B macros
Table, optional. Merged over
.BR [compile.macros] ;
on a key conflict the profile wins.
.TP
.B export_objs
Boolean or string, optional, default false. When enabled, a successful compile
of this profile also packs every project object file into an archive before
linking: true selects
.BR build/obj_files.zip ,
while a string is the archive path (relative to the project root) whose suffix
selects the format
.RB ( .zip ", " .tar.gz " or " .tgz ).
.SS [link]
.TP
.B flags
Array of strings, optional, default empty. Link flags.
.TP
.B msvc_flags
Array of strings, optional, default empty. MSVC\-only link flags.
.TP
.B link_dirs
Array of strings, optional, default empty.
.B \-L
search paths, relative to the project root.
.TP
.B system_target
Array of strings, optional, default empty. System libraries to link, for
example
.BR pthread " or " m .
Note the singular spelling: the key is
.BR system_target ,
not
.BR system_targets .
.SS [link.profile.<name>]
.TP
.B flags ", " msvc_flags
Array of strings, optional. Link flags appended after the base
.BR [link] flags.
.PP
A profile must exist under
.B [compile.profile.\fIname\fR]
as well: profile lookup consults the compile profiles, so a name defined only
here fails the build with an unknown\-profile error.
.SS [depends]
.TP
.B lib
Array of strings, optional, default empty. Hard dependencies. A missing
package is a fatal error at build time with an install hint.
.TP
.B want
Array of strings, optional, default empty. Optional dependencies. A missing
package only warns and defines an
.B EZMK_LIB_MISS_\fINAME\fR
macro so the code can degrade gracefully.
.TP
.B workspace
Array of strings, optional, default empty. Sibling members of the same
workspace to build first, by relative path or member name. The dependency
must be acyclic and the sibling must be of type
.BR static ;
version constraints are not supported here (see
.BR ezmk\-workspace.toml (5)).
.PP
Entries of
.B lib
and
.B want
may carry a version constraint, for example
.BR fmt ", " fmt@1.2.3 ", " fmt\(ha1.2.3 ", " "fmt\(ti1.2" ", " "fmt>=1.0" .
See
.BR "VERSION CONSTRAINTS" .
.SS [test]
.TP
.B dirs
Array of strings, optional, default
.BR ["test"] .
Directories holding test sources. An empty array falls back to the default. Like src_dirs, the search is flat by default; an entry ending in /** is searched recursively.
.TP
.B framework
String, optional, default
.BR catch2 .
Either
.B catch2
or the built\-in
.BR ezmk ;
the value is matched case\-insensitively, and anything else is an error.
.TP
.B default_profile
String, optional, default empty. Profile applied to the test build when
.B \-\-profile
is not given.
.TP
.B include_dirs
Array of strings, optional, default empty. Extra
.B \-I
directories for the test build only, relative to the project root.
.TP
.B link_targets
Array of strings, optional, default empty. Extra system libraries linked into
the test runner.
.TP
.B flags
Array of strings, deprecated. Use
.BR default_profile ", " include_dirs " and " link_targets .
Using it prints a deprecation warning; it is removed in 2.0.0.
.SS [hooks]
Lua scripts run around the build, with
.B ctx.output
.RB ( pre_build
only),
.B ctx.project_root
and
.BR ctx.profile .
.TP
.B pre_build
String, optional, default empty. Lua script executed before compilation.
.TP
.B post_build
String, optional, default empty. Lua script executed after a successful link.
.TP
.B on_failure
String, optional, default empty. Lua script executed when the
.B link
fails; a compile error does not trigger it.
.PP
Paths are relative to the project root. A missing script warns and is
skipped. Build hooks are the project's own code; install hooks are package code
and are gated by
.BR [utils.permissions] .
.SS [install]
.TP
.B prefix
String, optional. Install root. Default:
.B \(ti/.local
on Unix and
.B %LOCALAPPDATA%\eezmk
on Windows. A leading
.B \(ti/
or a lone
.B \(ti
is expanded to the home directory.
.TP
.B bindir
String, optional, default
.BR bin .
Subdirectory for executables and shared libraries.
.TP
.B libdir
String, optional, default
.BR lib .
Subdirectory for static libraries and import libraries.
.TP
.B includedir
String, optional, default
.BR include .
Subdirectory for headers, which are installed below
.BR includedir/\fIname\fR/ .
.TP
.B sharedir
String, optional, default
.BR share .
Reserved: it is parsed but no data files are installed yet, and
.B ezmk project install \-\-no\-data
has no effect.
.SS [utils]
.TP
.B tools
Array of strings, optional. Tool names provided by a
.B type = utils
package. The list is used for
.B ezmk pkg info
display only; tool lookup is filesystem\-based and looks for
.B utils/\fIname\fR.lua
inside installed packages.
.SS [utils.permissions]
Fine\-grained permissions for Lua tools and install hooks. Each key is an
array of path patterns or command names; the decision order is
.B deny
then
.B allow
then ask, and in a non\-interactive environment an unanswered request is
denied.
.TP
.B read ", " write
Array of strings, optional. Allowed read and write paths, relative to the
project root.
.TP
.B run
Array of strings, optional. Allowed commands; a trailing
.B *
matches by prefix.
.TP
.B read_deny ", " write_deny ", " run_deny
Array of strings, optional. Deny lists, which take precedence over the
corresponding allow list.
.TP
.B network
Boolean, optional, default
.BR false .
Declarative only: network access is recorded but not enforced yet.
.PP
A package that omits the whole
.B [utils.permissions]
section keeps the legacy unrestricted behaviour and prints a deprecation
warning on the first controlled access.
.SS [pkg]
.TP
.B strict_std_check
Boolean, optional, default
.BR false .
Turn the install\-time standard\-compatibility check into a fatal error when a
package requires a higher standard than
.BR [project].language .
.SH VERSION CONSTRAINTS
Entries in
.B [depends].lib
and
.B [depends].want
accept an optional constraint. The operators are
.BR >= ", " > ", " \(ha ", " \(ti " and " @ ,
and the earliest occurrence in the string wins; a constraint without a package
name is rejected, and the version part must be a numeric dotted version.
.TP
.B fmt
No constraint: the highest available version.
.TP
.B fmt@1.2.3
Exactly 1.2.3.
.TP
.B fmt>=1.0
At least 1.0.
.TP
.B fmt>1.0
Strictly greater than 1.0.
.TP
.B fmt\(ha1.2.3
Compatible: at least 1.2.3 and below the next major version
.RB ( <2.0.0 ).
.TP
.B fmt\(ti1.2.3
Approximate: at least 1.2.3 and below the next minor version
.RB ( <1.3.0 ).
.PP
Constraints are checked when packages are resolved and during the build; to
pin exact versions for reproducibility, commit
.BR ezmk.lock.json .
.SH DETERMINISTIC BUILDS
With
.B deterministic = true
EazyMake injects reproducible\-build flags (
.B \-ffile\-prefix\-map
and
.B \-frandom\-seed
for GCC and Clang,
.B /Brepro
for MSVC) and treats a missing or mismatched
.B ezmk.lock.json
as a fatal error; the lockfile hash also becomes part of the compile cache
signature. A pre\-1.4.5
.B ezmk.lock
(TOML) is still read, and the next
.B ezmk pkg install
migrates it.
.PP
The timestamp comes from the first of these that yields a value:
.BR [compile].source_date_epoch ,
the
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
environment variable, the git HEAD commit time, and finally the modification
time of
.BR ezmk.toml .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
.ft CR
[project]
name = "hello"
version = "0.1.0"
type = "executable"

[compile]
flags = ["\-Wall", "\-Wextra"]
default_profile = "debug"

[compile.profile.debug]
flags = ["\-g", "\-O0"]

[depends]
lib = ["fmt\(ha10.0"]

[test]
framework = "catch2"
dirs = ["test"]

[install]
prefix = "\(ti/.local"
.ft R
.fi
.SH RUNTIME CONFIGURATION
The user\-level and global
.B config.toml
files use a different schema from a project
.BR ezmk.toml :
they contain only the
.B [base_dir]
and
.B [settings]
tables. Project keys listed below never appear in those files.
.PP
The merge order is built\-in defaults, global
.BR config.toml ,
user
.BR config.toml ,
project
.BR ezmk.toml ,
then command\-line/environment overrides. Relative
.B [base_dir]
paths resolve against the directory containing the config file; a leading
.B \(ti
is expanded.
.SS [base_dir]
.TP
.B installed_packages
Directory for user/global scope package installations.
.TP
.B repo_cache
Directory for the user/global scope repository cache.
.TP
.B examples
Output root used by
.B ezmk example
when
.B \-o
is omitted.
.TP
.B logs
Directory for the optional
.B ezmk.log
file log.
.SS [settings]
.TP
.B natural_language
Interface language. Values are
.BR auto ,
.BR en ,
.B zh
or a variant tag. Precedence:
.BR \-\-lang ,
.BR EZMK_LANG ,
this key, system locale.
.TP
.B color_mode
One of
.BR auto ,
.BR off ,
.BR 16colors ,
.B 256colors
or
.BR truecolor .
.TP
.B color_theme
Reserved theme name; only
.B default
is accepted today.
.TP
.B log_level
One of
.BR off ,
.BR error ,
.BR warn ,
.B info
or
.BR debug .
.B fatal
messages are never filtered.
.TP
.B initial_commit
Boolean or string. Enables an initial
.B git commit
after
.B project new
created the repository; a string is used as the commit message.
.TP
.B auto_init_git
Boolean, default true. Run
.B git init
in
.BR "ezmk project new" .
.TP
.B gen_gitignore
Boolean, default true. Generate
.BR .gitignore .
.TP
.B gen_readme
Boolean, default true. Generate
.BR README.md .
.TP
.B gen_agent_md
Boolean, default false. Generate
.BR AGENTS.md .
.TP
.B default_project_type
Default
.B \-\-type
for
.BR "ezmk project new" .
.TP
.B default_language
Default language standard written into a new project.
.TP
.B default_project_version
Default project version written into a new project.
.TP
.B default_compile_flags
String array. Default
.B [compile].flags
written into a new project.
.TP
.B default_jobs
Non\-negative integer, default 0 (auto). Upper bound 1024. Overridden by
.BR [compile].jobs .
.TP
.B test_timeout
Integer seconds, default 30. Zero means no timeout. Overridden by
.BR [test].timeout .
.TP
.B test_report_dir
Default report directory. Overridden by
.BR [test].report_dir .
.TP
.B watch_debounce_ms
Zero (default 300) or 50..5000 milliseconds.
.TP
.B watch_ignore
String array of extra ignore prefixes.
.TP
.B pack_format
.BR tar.gz ,
.B zip
or the
.B tgz
alias.
.TP
.B pack_output_dir
Default pack output directory, relative to the process working directory.
.TP
.B pack_name
Archive basename; empty means
.BR <name>\-<version> .
.TP
.B pack_exclude
String array of extra directory names or extensions to exclude.
.TP
.B default_pkg_scope
.BR project ,
.B user
or
.BR global .
.TP
.B auto_install_deps
Boolean, default true. False makes a missing dependency fatal.
.TP
.B scan_skip_dirs
String array of extra directory names skipped by
.BR "workspace scan" .
.TP
.B git_path
Git executable path, default
.BR git .
.TP
.B editor
Editor command. EDITOR/VISUAL still take precedence.
.TP
.B auto_pack
Boolean, default false. Pack a static project after a successful build/run.
.SS Project run defaults
The following keys live in the project
.B ezmk.toml
and override the user/global defaults. They never appear in
.BR config.toml .
.TP
.B build_dir
Project build directory.
.TP
.B output_name
Artifact basename. Must be a safe basename.
.TP
.B jobs
Project parallelism; zero means auto; upper bound 1024.
.TP
.B timeout
Test timeout in seconds; zero means no timeout.
.TP
.B report_dir
Default test report directory.
.SS [watch]
.TP
.B debounce_ms
Zero (default 300) or 50..5000.
.TP
.B ignore
Extra ignore prefixes.
.SS [pack]
.TP
.B format
.BR tar.gz ,
.B zip
or
.BR tgz .
.TP
.B output_dir
Output directory, relative to the process working directory.
.TP
.B name
Archive basename.
.TP
.B exclude
Extra directory names or extensions to exclude.
.SS [pkg]
.TP
.B auto_install
Boolean. False fails on a missing dependency instead of installing it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ezmk (1)
.PP
The full specification, the package authoring guide and the CLI reference ship
with the source tree as
.BR docs/en/project_config.md ", " docs/en/package_authoring.md " and " docs/en/cli.md .
